{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RETRACTION -- THIS TICKET IS FACTUALLY WRONG AS FILED, and I filed it. Verified against current main in a venv worktree rather than from memory.\n\nMY CLAIM WAS: 'a mechanism-ok marker satisfies --check but NOT tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py, which asserts new == 0 and set(baseline) == live REGARDLESS of markers, and every route to the baseline is forbidden to contributors -- therefore no justified mechanism is landable.'\n\nBOTH ASSERTIONS ACTUALLY HONOUR MARKERS. Read them:\n  test_check_passes_on_the_committed_tree:\n      assert \"new=0\" in out or \"admitted\" in out\n  test_the_committed_baseline_matches_the_live_tree (line 349):\n      assert set(baseline) | admitted == live\nThe first passes on an 'admitted' line; the second adds the admitted set explicitly. So a correctly\nmarked mechanism needs no baseline entry and no maintenance command.\n\nPROOF ON CURRENT MAIN: the scanner-integration workflow carries two ci_gate markers, the committed\nbaseline contains ZERO scanner entries (grep -c = 0), --check reports 'active=682 new=2 increased=0\nstale=0' with BOTH lines marked 'admitted', and both assertions PASS. That is precisely the situation\nthis ticket says is impossible.\n\nWHAT ACTUALLY HAPPENED WITH CHANGE 2601 is narrower and I over-generalised from it. Its failure was:\n  FAILED test_check_passes_on_the_committed_tree - AssertionError: active=682 new=1 increased=0 stale=0\nNote the output has NO 'admitted' line. Its marker was NOT matched by markers_for -- compare.py:95\nrequires a marker for the EXACT key. So the real question is why that one marker did not match\n(placement or parse), not whether markers work at all. We never diagnosed it, because that agent\nrestructured to avoid the mechanism entirely -- partly on my say-so.\n\nTHE COST OF MY ERROR, recorded because it changed real decisions:\n - Change 2601 restructured its design to dodge a mechanism it may not have needed to dodge. The\n   restructure is defensible on its own merits (repairing the existing guard is narrower than adding\n   a second one beside it) but it was chosen under a false constraint.\n - The S6 agent DECLINED to add the REBAR_GATE_MAX_CONCURRENT env tier that ADR 0112 asks for,\n   citing this contradiction, and documented the omission as a deviation to be revisited 'once a1f1\n   is fixed'. There is nothing to fix, so that tier can simply be added with a correct marker.\n - Every subagent brief tonight carried 'you cannot land a new mechanism -- STOP and report'. That\n   instruction was wrong and is now withdrawn.\n\nRESCOPING THIS TICKET rather than closing it outright: there IS a real, much smaller defect here --\na marker can silently fail to match its key, and when it does, the failure message says 'new=1' with\nno hint that a marker was present but rejected. That is a bad diagnostic for an easy mistake.\nProposed replacement acceptance criteria:\n 1. A mechanism-ok marker that does not match any detected key produces a diagnostic naming the\n    marker, the key it was parsed as, and the keys actually detected -- rather than silently leaving\n    the mechanism unadmitted.\n 2. Reproduce 2601's exact marker and determine why it was not admitted; fix the cause if it is a\n    parser/placement defect, or document the rule if the marker was genuinely malformed.\n 3. docs/architecture.md's 'Mechanism-delta ratchet' section states marker placement per detection\n    shape unambiguously, since ci_gate has TWO shapes (scripts/check_*.py named by path, and workflow\n    run: steps named by file::step) and they plainly do not take a marker in the same place.\n 4. Defect-seeded: a deliberately malformed marker makes AC1's diagnostic fire."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788508928029403001,"uuid":"81ccf769-1c80-4316-8e57-f50e2346730e"}